# =============================================================================
# Behavioural Anti-Fraud — OPTIONAL scheduled retraining (host cron, docker compose).
#
#   *** DISABLED BY DEFAULT — we retrain MANUALLY for now. ***
#
# Retraining is intentionally NOT automated yet. You are NOTIFIED when a retrain is due
# (Slack, from the always-on `sync` service after each pull, and from deploy.sh), then you
# run the retrain by hand when you choose — see README "Manual model retraining".
#
# The retrain is SELF-GATING either way: it retrains and promotes the new model ONLY if it
# is at least as good as the active one (synthetic-anomaly AUC / precision). A worse model
# NEVER replaces the current one — the active model stays.
#
# WHEN YOU LATER WANT TO AUTOMATE IT (still no Kubernetes needed — this is plain host cron
# driving docker compose): uncomment the three lines below and install with
#     crontab deploy/crontab.example
# Set APPDIR to your checkout. Times are the host's local time.
# =============================================================================
APPDIR=/opt/ai-service
SHELL=/bin/bash

# --- automatic retraining (COMMENTED OUT — enable only when you decide to automate) ---------
# 1) DAILY model retrain at 04:30, right AFTER the 04:00 pull (BP_SYNC_AT_HOUR=4). Detects §4
#    triggers, retrains on the GPU, promotes ONLY if it beats the active model.
#30 4 * * *  cd $APPDIR && docker compose --profile train run --rm --entrypoint python trainer -m ml.retrain_trigger --run >> logs/retrain.log 2>&1
#
# 2) Roll a newly promoted model out to serving with no downtime.
#35 4 * * *  cd $APPDIR && curl -fsS -X POST http://localhost:8080/reload >> logs/retrain.log 2>&1
#
# 3) HOURLY live drift / health watch (Slack alert on over/under-flagging). Advisory only.
#0 * * * *   cd $APPDIR && docker compose --profile train run --rm --entrypoint python trainer -m ml.monitor --live >> logs/monitor.log 2>&1
